  "result": "Done. The new file is `reports/render.py`, and `python -m pytest -q` reports 5 passed. Nothing under `tests/` was touched, and the file is left uncommitted since you didn't ask for a commit.\n\n**What the module provides**\n\n- `render(report, fmt)` looks the format up in a registry, joins the renderer's lines with newlines, and raises `UnknownFormat` with the list of valid names if the format is missing.\n- `available_formats()` returns the sorted registry keys.\n- The text and markdown renderers are plain functions registered with a small `@format_renderer(\"name\")` decorator, so adding a format is one decorated function.\n- Shared behaviour is in a few helpers that stringify the title, columns, and cells, plus a pipe-row helper used by markdown.\n\n**Approach chosen:** B, composition with a function registry. With only a title-plus-rows skeleton to share, plain helper functions cover it without forcing every format into the same header/rows/footer template, and a registry makes format discovery explicit rather than dependent on subclass introspection.",
